## Test Categorization

Specs are organized into three physical categories under `spec/`:

| Category | Directory | When to use |
|----------|-----------|-------------|
| **Unit** | `spec/unit/` | Pure logic, no I/O, no external state |
| **Integration** | `spec/integration/` | Touches filesystem, Store, Dir.mktmpdir |
| **Conformance** | `spec/conformance/` | String-described specs asserting contract behavior |

The `spec_helper` derives tag (`:unit`, `:integration`, `:conformance`) from file path — no hand-maintained tags.

## Spec Layout Conventions

- Files mirror `lib/` namespace, placed under the correct category dir
- Unit specs are pure: no filesystem, no Store construction
- Conformance specs use string descriptions (not `describe MyClass`)
- The `SpecLayout` guard enforces these rules at load time

## Shared Infrastructure

### Fixtures (`spec/support/fixtures.rb`)
- `store_from_manifest()` — builds Store with manifest, lanes, schemas, seed files
- `minimal_store()`, `machine_store()`, `workflow_store()` — preset builders
- `test_ctx(role:, correlation_id:, dry_run:)` — builds `Value::Call`
- `converge_now()` — runs convergence
- `with_missing_workflows()` — auto-creates passthrough workflows for publish targets

### Matchers (`spec/support/matchers.rb`)
- `have_audit_verb(verb).with_correlation(cid)` — queries audit event store
- `be_success` / `be_failure` — result matchers

### Shared Contexts
- `"textus_store_fixture"` — tempdir + cleanup
- `"cli invocation"` — StringIO triple + CLI.run wrapper
- `"conformance fixture"` — full textus/4 store (all lanes, schemas)
- `"core domain"` — domain doubles (fake_clock, fake_file_stat)

### Shared Examples
- `"a canon-write refused"` — asserts `WriteForbidden`
- `"an audited write"` — records verb in audit log
- `"a correlated write"` — propagates correlation_id

## Fixture Vocabulary

Zone names, kinds, and key namespaces are defined once in `spec/support/fixtures.rb`. Specs reference the vocabulary rather than re-spelling literals, reducing churn when names change.

## Coverage

Coverage is opt-in via `COVERAGE=1`. Baseline targets: line 93%, branch 75%.

Specs may only be retired when they drop zero unique line/branch coverage, with each citing its coverage delta.

## Disabled RuboCop RSpec Rules (intentional)

- `RSpec/DescribeClass` — house style uses full `Textus::` constants
- `RSpec/DescribedClass` — full path preferred for clarity
- `RSpec/NamedSubject` — bare `subject` used extensively
- `RSpec/SpecFilePathFormat` — files don't 1:1 mirror class names
- `RSpec/ContextWording` — noun phrases used in shared contexts
